# The console's build context is `./frontend` (see docker-compose.yml), so the
# repository-root .dockerignore does not apply here. Docker reads the
# .dockerignore at the root of the context it was given, and nowhere else.
#
# Without this file `COPY . .` runs *after* `npm ci` and copies the host's
# `node_modules` straight over the one the image just installed. The host is
# Windows and the image is Alpine, so that replaces Linux binaries for esbuild
# and rollup with Windows ones - a build that either fails confusingly or
# succeeds with the wrong artefacts. It also shipped a few hundred megabytes to
# the daemon on every build.
node_modules/
dist/

# Never needed to build, and `npm run build` would not look at them anyway.
.vite/
coverage/
*.log
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Editor and VCS noise.
.git/
.DS_Store
